[3] GATE 1b: does the u-coupled MATTER sector feed back into PPN? (sympy closed forms + numbers)
====================================================================================================
    Structure: every operator the MI functional adds to the worldline dynamics carries a factor
    eps(x) = 1/mu(x) - 1 or its derivative; u-frame velocity w enters only by DRESSING the
    mu-argument: x -> x(1 + kappa_w w^2/c^2), kappa_w = O(1). The preferred-frame (alpha_1-type)
    coefficient generated in the matter sector is therefore  ~ |x eps'(x)| * kappa_w  at the
    acceleration x of the test body. Sympy closed forms:
      exp tail  : x*d(eps)/dx = -sqrt(x)*exp(sqrt(x))/(2*exp(2*sqrt(x)) - 4*exp(sqrt(x)) + 2)
                  (= -(sqrt(x)/2) e^(-sqrt(x))/(1-e^(-sqrt(x)))^2 -- exponentially dead)
      power tail: x*d(eps)/dx = -1/(x*sqrt(x**2 + 1))   (~ -1/x^2 at large x)

    effective matter-side alpha_1-type coefficient |x eps'(x)| (kappa_w=1):
